<section class="section section--white" aria-labelledby="s1-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="split__aside">
        <h2 class="split__title rv" id="s1-title">AI Agent Security Testing for Autonomous, Tool-Using AI Systems</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split__body prose">
        <p class="rv">AI agents plan their own steps and use tools to carry them out: they send messages, query databases, update records, browse the web and run code. That autonomy is what makes them useful, and it is also what changes the risk. A flaw that would only make a chatbot say something wrong can make an agent do something wrong, with the permissions you gave it.</p>
        <p class="rv">CipherTrivia's AI agent security testing examines the agent as a whole: the instructions that steer it, the untrusted content it reads, the tools and credentials it holds, the approvals that supervise it and the systems it can reach. We try to mislead it, push it past its limits and abuse its tools, and we show exactly what an attacker could achieve.</p>
        <p class="rv">The aim is a smaller blast radius. Our findings help you give each agent only the access its job requires, enforce those limits outside the prompt, and keep a record of what the agent did.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

