<section class="section section--paper" id="types" aria-labelledby="s2-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="shead">
      <div class="shead__meta"></div>
      <div class="shead__body">
        <h2 class="shead__title rv" id="s2-title">Our AI Agent Security Testing Services</h2>
        <p class="shead__lede rv" style="--d:1">Each engagement is scoped to your agent and the systems it can reach. These are the areas we test, from the instructions that guide the agent to the approvals that supervise it.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="ledger">
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("escalate") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Agent Permission and Privilege Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We inventory what the agent is allowed to do and test whether it holds more access than its task needs. Findings show where permissions can be reduced and where limits are enforced only by the prompt.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("terminal") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Tool and Function Abuse Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We test whether an attacker can make the agent call a tool with harmful parameters, call tools in a damaging order, or use a legitimate tool for an unintended purpose.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("key") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Agent Identity and Credential Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We review how the agent authenticates, whose identity it acts under, how tokens and API keys are stored and scoped, and whether an agent's access can be reused or impersonated.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:3">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("syringe") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Indirect Prompt Injection Testing for Agents</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We plant hostile instructions in the pages, files, tickets and messages your agent reads, and test whether they can redirect it. Agents read a great deal of untrusted content, so this is a core test.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("target") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Goal Hijacking and Task Manipulation Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We try to change what the agent is trying to achieve, through conversation, poisoned context or conflicting instructions, and check whether it keeps to its intended purpose.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("link") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">MCP and Integration Security Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">For agents that connect through Model Context Protocol servers, plugins or custom connectors, we test how tools are described and authorized and whether tool output can smuggle in instructions.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("network") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Multi-Agent and Memory Security Testing</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We test how agents trust one another and whether a compromised agent can instruct another. We also check whether shared memory and context can be poisoned to affect later decisions.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:3">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("user-shield") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Human-in-the-Loop and Approval Control Review</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">We test whether approvals for sensitive actions can be bypassed, whether the approval request shows what will really happen, and whether a reviewer can be misled or overwhelmed.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

