<section class="section section--white" id="threats" aria-labelledby="s3-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="shead">
      <div class="shead__meta"></div>
      <div class="shead__body">
        <h2 class="shead__title rv" id="s3-title">Agentic AI Threats Our Testing Covers</h2>
        <p class="shead__lede rv" style="--d:1">Agents introduce risks beyond those of a plain language model. Our test coverage follows recognized agentic AI threat guidance, alongside the OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications, so findings use terms your security and engineering teams already know.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="ledger ledger--10">
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("database") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Memory Poisoning</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">False or hostile information written into an agent's memory that shapes its later decisions.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("wrench") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Tool Misuse</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Legitimate tools driven into harmful use through manipulated instructions or parameters.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("unlock") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Privilege Compromise</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">An agent's access abused or widened to reach data and actions it was never meant to touch.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("gauge") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Resource Overload</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Tasks that push an agent into runaway loops, heavy tool use or very large costs.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("alert") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Cascading Hallucination</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">A false statement that is stored, repeated and acted on until it spreads through connected agents and systems.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("target") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Intent Breaking and Goal Manipulation</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Attempts to redirect an agent's plan or objective away from what its owner intended.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("document") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Repudiation and Untraceability</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Agent actions that are not logged well enough to show who or what caused them.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("identity") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Identity Spoofing and Impersonation</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Attackers posing as a user, an agent or a trusted service to borrow its authority.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("users-cross") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Overwhelming Human Oversight</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Floods of approval requests or misleading summaries that make human review ineffective.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("code") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Unexpected Code Execution</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Agents that can run code or commands being steered into executing an attacker's instructions.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

