<section class="section section--ink" aria-labelledby="s5-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="process">
      <div class="process__aside">
        <h2 class="process__title" id="s5-title">Our AI Agent Security Testing Process</h2>
        <p class="process__lede">Every engagement starts by mapping what the agent can do, then tests how far an attacker could take it. Testing is planned with your team so that real actions are exercised safely.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="process__list" data-process>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Scope and Agent Architecture Mapping</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We map how the agent is built: its model, instructions, memory, data sources and the systems it connects to. We agree what is in scope and which actions may be exercised for real.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Tool, Permission and Identity Inventory</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We list every tool the agent can call, the permissions and credentials behind each one, and the identity it acts under. This inventory shows the agent's potential blast radius before any attack begins.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Injection and Goal Hijacking Attacks</h3>
          <p class="step__text">Testers attempt direct and indirect prompt injection and try to redirect the agent's goals, using content the agent reads in normal operation: pages, files, tickets and messages.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Action and Boundary Testing</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We test whether the agent can be made to exceed its permissions, misuse its tools, bypass approvals or act on another user's behalf, and whether limits are enforced outside the prompt.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Risk Analysis and Reporting</h3>
          <p class="step__text">Each finding is validated, reproduced and rated by severity and business impact. The report explains the attack path in plain terms and recommends a specific fix for each issue.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Remediation Support and Retesting</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We walk your team through the findings and support fixes as they are built. After remediation we retest to confirm each boundary now holds and that the changes have not opened new gaps.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

